The stereo layer is active only once the compositor took its declaration, and a failed declaration is said (ORDER 448). The layer attached and committed the two views of a 3D video even when the declaration of its surface as stereo content failed (a warning in the log only), and stereoLayerActive never looked at the declaration: the person saw the packed frame, both views side by side in each eye, while the player said 3D. The surface is now declared when the layer is made, before any buffer is attached to it, and a refusal is kept for the layer's life: a layer whose declaration failed attaches and commits nothing on any of its three routes (window surface, own DMA-BUF buffers, wl_shm), its presenter is not valid and says why, and VideoOutput does not use it. stereoLayerActive is then false, the item draws the video through the scene graph (one view, by stereoView), and the new read-only VideoOutput and Video property stereoLayerFailure holds the reason, with its change signal; the reason is also logged once (category qt.multimedia.video.stereolayer). It stays while the same 3D video plays, so the declaration is not asked for again at every frame, and clears when the 3D video ends or the item changes window: the next 3D video declares again. The other failures to make the layer on a compositor that announces the stereo global are said the same way, through stereoLayerFailure and one log line, and no presenter is made again for them while the same 3D video plays (they were silent, and asked again at every timer tick): the window without a wl_surface, the declaration library that could not start (stereo_declare_wayland_init busy, say), the library that did not take the announced global (stereo_supported_wayland false), and the window without an alpha buffer. A compositor that announces no stereo global is a 2D desktop, not a failure.

Opening the next file no longer aborts a player that plays NVDEC video through the scene graph's render thread (ORDER 496, patch 0047). The CUDA texture converter (Qt dev's, patch 0033) made the OpenGL context current to delete its textures, from whichever thread let go the last reference to the decoder's frames context: a player that opens another file closes the decoder on the GUI thread, and Qt answered "Cannot make QOpenGLContext current in a different thread" with an abort (exit 134), at some source changes and not at others (Plank Player with a half side by side file, every time). The converter now makes the context current only on the context's own thread; on another it gives its planes (the textures and their CUDA registrations, which CUDA refuses to unregister without the texture's context current, error 219) to the context's share group, which frees them when one of its contexts is next made current, as Qt does for its own textures, and a failed unregistration is now said. tst_qffmpegcudatextureconverter releases the frames context on the context's thread and on another one.

A plain 3D video stays on the GPU through the stereo layer (ORDER 500, patch 0048). The layer's presenter drew the views into the compositor's window surface only for the drawn views of a depth video; every other 3D video, a plain full side by side file included, was read back from the decoder's frames, converted on the processor and copied into wl_shm buffers, about 250 to 280 percent of one core for a 3840x1080 clip at 30 frames a second on AMD and on NVIDIA. A frame of the decoder's textures (VA-API, CUDA) is now taken apart by the GPU where it is: one pass for each view converts its samples to RGB at the content's depth (8 bits, or 16 bits above) into one texture, the first view of the packing at the left and each view at the size its samples have, for every packing of H.264 Table D-8, H.265 Table D.8 and RFC 9559's StereoMode that the layer unpacks (side by side and top and bottom, half or full, rows, columns, checkerboard, quincunx, frame sequence); nothing is interpolated or resized. The drawing context asks EGL for no reset notification, because the layer's own context shares it and EGL refuses a share list of contexts with different notification strategies (EGL_BAD_MATCH). The layer draws that texture into its window surface as it does the drawn views, with the crop and the eye order. A frame the GPU cannot take apart (decoded by the processor, a pixel format the passes do not read, a converter that refuses the DMA-BUF) is still copied into wl_shm buffers, and the presenter's log (qt.multimedia.video.stereopresenter) says why; A layer that refuses the views of a depth (NVIDIA 615 has no 16 bit unsigned window surface, and the compositor lists no XB48 modifier) is asked again every sixtieth frame, and the frames in between are copied at once with the reason. QT_MM_STEREO_LAYER_SHM=1 still asks for the copy. tst_qquickvideostereo gains plainPackingsOnTheGpu (every packing at 8, 10, 12 and 16 bit words, the views predicted from the packing, no read back) and plainFramesTheGpuCannotTake and plainViewsAreSharedByTheLayersContext.

